  "id": "RLSA-2026:98588",
  "title": "Moderate: openssl security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-13 12:06:37"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-19 12:06:52"
  },
  "severity": "Moderate",
  "description": "OpenSSL is a toolkit that implements the Secure Sockets Layer (SSL) and Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocols, as well as a full-strength general-purpose cryptography library.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* openssl: openssl: Denial of Service via excessive memory allocation in CRL distribution point processing (CVE-2026-35189)\n\n* openssl: openssl: Denial of Service via excessive QUIC packet buffer retention (CVE-2026-54873)\n\n* openssl: openssl: Denial of Service via crafted CMP certificate revocation response (CVE-2026-75805)\n\n* openssl: openssl: Denial of Service via inefficient QUIC stream reassembly (CVE-2026-42772)\n\n* openssl: OpenSSL: Private key recovery via timing side-channel in generic elliptic curve operations (CVE-2026-54872)\n\n* openssl: OpenSSL: Denial of Service via unenforced QUIC connection flow control (CVE-2026-75804)\n\n* openssl: openssl: information disclosure via non-constant-time SM2 scalar multiplication on ARM64 and RISC-V (CVE-2026-54875)\n\n* openssl: openssl: Traffic amplification Denial of Service via QUIC packet over-accounting (CVE-2026-35191)\n\n* openssl: OpenSSL: Private key recovery via SM2 timing side-channel (CVE-2026-77696)\n\n* openssl: openssl: Denial of Service via out-of-bounds write during TLS context switch (CVE-2026-72897)\n\n* openssl: OpenSSL: Denial of Service via undersized DTLS record (CVE-2026-75806)\n\n* openssl: OpenSSL: Denial of Service via unbounded QUIC connection identifier backlog (CVE-2026-84784)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* [Rocky Linux 10.3]OpenSSL silently uses default provider when `fips.so` is missing on systems in FIPS mode (JIRA:Rocky Linux-213740)\n\n* OpenSSL fails to initialize when automatic initialization happens in threads (JIRA:Rocky Linux-252344)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
